    <text:h text:outline-level="1">Appendix B: Glossary</text:h>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Block.</text:span><text:s/>A paragraph, heading or list item in a text document.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Bookmark.</text:span><text:s/>A name attached to a place in a text document. It keeps pointing at the same place when you edit above it.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Cell.</text:span><text:s/>One box in a spreadsheet, named by its column and row.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Flat file.</text:span><text:s/>An ODF document saved as one plain text file, such as <text:span text:style-name="T2">.fods</text:span><text:s/>or <text:span text:style-name="T2">.fodt</text:span>.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Formula.</text:span><text:s/>An entry in a cell that starts with <text:span text:style-name="T2">=</text:span><text:s/>and calculates a value.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Lint.</text:span><text:s/>An automatic check of a document for mistakes.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Locale.</text:span><text:s/>The set of conventions a document follows for numbers, such as which character is the decimal point.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">ODF.</text:span><text:s/>OpenDocument Format, the open standard grind uses for its files.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Package.</text:span><text:s/>An ODF document saved as a compressed archive, such as <text:span text:style-name="T2">.ods</text:span><text:s/>or <text:span text:style-name="T2">.odt</text:span>.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Palette.</text:span><text:s/>The searchable list of commands that opens with Ctrl+K.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Template.</text:span><text:s/>A document that provides the page, the letterhead and the styles for others.</text:p>
  </office:text>
 </office:body>
</office:document>
